  "body": "## What changed\nA Go home as the **last** entry was written twice: once as the entry, then again as the post's own end-of-program home before `M30` (found in the hands-on check of #469).\n\n**Seam: each post's own script.** The posts differ, so an app-level drop would be wrong. Siemens' end-of-program home is `G53 Z0` only, Fanuc writes `G49` before a trip home under TCPM, and the lathe homes X then Z.\n- **New PRELUDE helper:** `linesWritten()`, documented in `docs/CNC-INTERMEDIATE.md`.\n- **In each script:** the trip home records `homedAt`, and `onClose()` writes its own home only if a line was written since. In every post the trip home covers at least what the end-of-program home does.\n- **Covered:** Fanuc, Haas, Mazak, Siemens 840D and Fanuc Lathe. Heidenhain and Tormach already refuse a trip home by name.\n- **Unchanged:** mid-program homes, Suppress and \"Skip pauses and homes\".\n- **Decision record:** `docs/decisions/504-trailing-home.md`.\n\n**Fanuc tail:**\n```\nbefore            after\nG91 G28 Z0        G91 G28 Z0\nG28 X0 Y0         G28 X0 Y0\nG90               G90\nG91 G28 Z0        M30\nG28 X0 Y0\nM30\n```\n\n## How tested\n- **New tests (`program_entry`):**\n  - `a_trailing_home_entry_merges_with_the_program_end_home` (Fanuc, Haas, Mazak, Siemens 840D): one home for a trailing Go home; suppressed and skipped homes match the plain program; a mid-program home still gives two.\n  - `the_lathe_post_writes_a_trailing_home_once`.\n  - Both failed before the fix.\n- **Goldens updated:** `program_entry/fanuc_pause_home.nc` and the Haas golden; each lost the duplicate home.\n- **Gate:** the 31 app suites covering the posts (program_entry, posting, conformance, after_op, golden_cl, per_op_files, and the fanuc, lathe, tormach, inverted, coolant and probe post suites) and all camcraft-post tests pass. Clippy is clean.\n\n## Not exercised\nA machine or simulator run. The change only removes a duplicate home at program end.\n\nChangelog: A Go home as the last entry is written once: it merges with the post's end-of-program home (Fanuc, Haas, Mazak, Siemens 840D, Fanuc Lathe) (#504)\n\nFixes #504\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
